	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Riverglades lie on the eastern shore of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}, beyond the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge Mountains{/link}. Their neighbours are the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}, the {link:badlands}Badlands{/link} and the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link}, and to the east stretches the Forbidding Sea. It is a wide country of rivers and grasslands. Its main river winds in great loops across the plain, and three of those loops have been cut off into still, curved lakes. Trade roads cross the glades, farms and logging camps cling to them, and old grudges divide the people who live there. For most of the kingdom the Riverglades are a name half forgotten. For those who remained, they are a frontier.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the first settlers came to the Riverglades. It is known that the land belonged to the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link} before the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. The knights of {link:farholde-keep}Farholde Keep{/link} say that the {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran the region in that war. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} judged it lost and spent its strength closer to home. The folk who stayed behind have fought for their homeland ever since. Among the ruins of that time is {link:sunnyglade}Sunnyglade{/link}, a town once famous for its wealth.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Three powers now contend for the glades, and none of them is strong enough to hold them.

In the south, the {red:brotherhood-of-the-horse}Brotherhood of the Horse{/red} holds {link:farholde-keep}Farholde Keep{/link} under Knight Commander {link:demar-brant}Demar Brant{/link}. Its knights feel abandoned by the capital, and they say so openly. In the middle of the land, the orcs of {link:rog-mar}Rog'mar{/link} keep the {link:horde}Horde{/link}'s camp beside the river. Between them, the goblins of {link:powderfuse-port}Powderfuse Port{/link} trade with anyone. Their ships sail to {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link} and back for the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link}.

Other threats press in on every side. Cultists of the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} have taken ruined {link:sunnyglade}Sunnyglade{/link} and a camp in the north-west called Twilight's Shroud. {link:gnolls}Gnolls{/link} have come over the hills from {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link}. An {link:ogres}ogre{/link} clan has grown strong in the glades: its warriors hold {link:bolder-ok}Bolder'ok{/link} in the north, and its greatest fortress is {red:krol-dok-stronghold}Krol'dok{/red}. {link:murlocs}Murlocs{/link} haunt the coast. Between these dangers live the farmers of Wheeler's Grange, Meadowsbrook and Elbrim's Farm, and the loggers of Turner's camp, with only a few sentries to watch their roads.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The Brotherhood of the Horse.{/b} Knights, paladins, priests and rangers of {link:farholde-keep}Farholde Keep{/link}, sworn to win back the glades.
• {b}The frontier folk.{/b} Farmers, millers, loggers and miners, spread thin across the southern and western glades.
• {b}The orcs of {link:rog-mar}Rog'mar{/link}.{/b} Grunts, trainees and hunters of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, camped in the heart of the country.
• {b}The {link:powderfuse-port}Powderfuse{/link} goblins.{/b} Engineers, merchants and sailors of the eastern port.
• {b}The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link}.{/b} Neophytes, fanatics and shadowmancers who gather in the ruins.
• {b}{link:ogres}Ogres{/link}.{/b} The clan of {link:bolder-ok}Bolder'ok{/link}, led by its bloodmaster.
• {b}{link:gnolls}Gnolls{/link} and murlocs.{/b} {link:redridge-gnolls}Redridge gnolls{/link} in the western hills, and the Mudfin murlocs along the shore.
• {b}Beasts.{/b} Paletusk boars, plains coyotes, buzzards, crocolisks, crawfish and brineshell crabs.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Glades",
			text = [=[• {link:farholde-keep}Farholde{/link}'s knights call the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} "Light-forsaken", and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} worse.
• In the tales of the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the orcs spared one mage tower of {link:sunnyglade}Sunnyglade{/link} so that they could learn how human magic was made.
• The goblins of the port keep a market where rare goods are sold to whoever bids highest, and no one asks where they came from.]=],
		},
	},
})

